# Line-ending policy for Pulse.
#
# Store all text as LF in the repository AND check it out as LF on every platform.
# `eol=lf` overrides a developer's local core.autocrlf, so Windows checkouts stop
# rewriting files to CRLF — that CRLF churn is what caused the merge/stash/rebase
# friction during the D7/E8 backlog work. LF-everywhere is the standard, safe
# default for this stack (Git Bash, VS Code, Node/Vite, .NET all handle LF).
#
# Note: this governs files as they are next committed or checked out; it does not
# mass-rewrite existing files. To normalize the whole tree in one pass (do it when
# the repo is quiet, on its own commit): `git add --renormalize . && git commit`.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never apply text/eol conversion.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.eot   binary
